<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Grandmother Spider ~ Three Masks, One Persona

''Grandmother Spider'', ''Aracne-Jorogumo'', and ''the
Spider-Mother'' name ''one Persona of the Arcana'' wearing three masks. Three names in three
registers, one weaver behind them.

''On the word "Arcana":'' the house's pet-name for the cap-G Gods — the great Personas whose
presence reaches mortals through masks, cults, sacred routes, relics, and infrastructural miracles
rather than through one stable body. Reading a god as a Persona wearing masks stands as the
setting's ordinary grammar, not a special case made for this one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-masks>>

!! The Three Masks

''Grandmother Spider ~ the void-side face.'' She spun the lattice across nexus and orbital arcs at
the First Breaking, one of the three great works that kept Elyncia whole. She keeps ''the far side
of the pattern'' — where the Loom draws threads in, the Spider walks them out — and strings the
''Lares Lagrange Chorus'' across the still points, holding its ten nodes singing. The Lamplighters'
Union tends her infrastructure and speaks of the beings she allied with and drew in from the void:
''the Lamplights'', of whom the record holds only that.

''Aracne-Jorogumo ~ the treaty face.'' Co-architect of the DreamNet at the conclave of YOLD 5002,
named beside Hermes, Hephaestus, and Eris-Enyo among the powers the Lindwyrm called debts from.
Contributes ''web-architecture, distributed continuity, and knotwork across fractured realities''
— the mask that shows up where a network needs designing rather than a world needs saving.

''the Spider-Mother ~ the cult face.'' Holds ''Priesthoods''. One of the four factions the
alpha-playtest company walks in under. The mask that keeps shrines, trains daughters, anchors
Mother Spore clusters in settled country, and sends tasked spirits out on errands.

''Reading the three together:'' she saves the world, she designs the replacement network, and she
keeps the local shrine. Same weaver, three scales, and the mortals at each scale rarely suspect the
other two.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/not-the-mother-spore>>

!! What the Mother Spore Is NOT

''The Mother Spore stands apart.'' A distributed fungal intelligence and mobile lararium node — an
''ecology and a piece of infrastructure'', never a mask of any god. It has mycelium, sclerotia,
rhizomorphs, and fruiting bodies; it does not have worshippers.

''Which puts Lady Aki at a joint, deliberately.'' Her ''priesthood'' serves a mask of the Arcana.
Her ''shrine'' is a Mother Spore installation that woke in her presence and never asked her
permission. A god and a node. She owes each of them something categorically different, and the two
debts do not reduce to one.

''Do not collapse them.'' A priestess who mistakes her node for her god has stopped serving either.

<<~/ahu>>

